OwnTV: open a MediaCodec video decoder that renders to a surface with max-width / max-height.

Why: FFmpeg configures the decoder with mime, size and csd only. ExoPlayer and the platform players
also pass max-width/max-height, which asks for adaptive playback. On the TCL (Realtek C2 AVC decoder)
H.264 opened without them was set up in "native buffer" mode: its frames went through the GPU
(SurfaceFlinger CLIENT composition, no video-plane session), and every H.264 channel above 30 fps
was presented at exactly 30 fps on mpv (each frame held two refreshes) while mpv itself reported no
drops. With them the decoder takes its direct video-out path (DVO, as under ExoPlayer and as HEVC
already did): 1080p50 30.0 -> 50.0 fps, 1080p59.94 30.0 -> 57.8-59.2 fps.

The keys are the documented MediaFormat ones every ExoPlayer session already sends on every device;
a decoder without adaptive playback ignores them. Only with a surface (mpv's direct path): the copy
path, which catch-up uses, opens exactly as before. At least 1920x1080, so an SD or 720p stream that
steps up to HD mid-way stays within the declared maximum.

Drop it once FFmpeg's decoder sets them itself. Test: H.264 1080p50/59.94, 720p50, SD, HEVC 4K HDR and
a film on mpv — presented fps (SurfaceFlinger), the decoder's "DVO_ANB" port mode in logcat.

diff --git a/libavcodec/mediacodecdec_common.c b/libavcodec/mediacodecdec_common.c
index 9a627c0..e1b3050 100644
--- a/libavcodec/mediacodecdec_common.c
+++ b/libavcodec/mediacodecdec_common.c
@@ -847,6 +847,15 @@ int ff_mediacodec_dec_init(AVCodecContext *avctx, MediaCodecDecContext *s,
     if (ret < 0)
         goto fail;
 
+    if (avctx->codec_type == AVMEDIA_TYPE_VIDEO && s->surface) {
+        /* Adaptive playback, as the platform's own players open a decoder that renders to a
+         * surface: some decoders choose their direct output path from it and fall back to a slower
+         * one without it. At least 1080p, so a stream that steps up to HD mid-way stays within it;
+         * decoders without adaptive playback ignore the keys. */
+        ff_AMediaFormat_setInt32(format, "max-width", FFMAX(avctx->width, 1920));
+        ff_AMediaFormat_setInt32(format, "max-height", FFMAX(avctx->height, 1080));
+    }
+
     status = ff_AMediaCodec_configure(s->codec, format, s->surface, NULL, 0);
     if (status < 0) {
         char *desc = ff_AMediaFormat_toString(format);
